From 1379a29467cc6a5a439765bd21cadf6f000ae3c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Majid Arasskhani <M.Arasskhani@gosilkroad.net>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 22:01:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/12] refactor(chat): stream_chat's finally block becomes
 turn_settlement.settle_turn
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Second step of the split. The 190-line shielded ``finally`` inside
stream_chat — capacity release, persister.finalize, memory-usage records,
RequestLog + ledger + hold settlement with retries, Agent run finalization
and the ``alpha_router`` metadata trailer — is now
``turn_settlement.settle_turn(identity, outcome, ...)`` with two explicit
dataclasses (`TurnIdentity`: who/what/where; `TurnOutcome`: what the
stream produced). stream_chat still owns the shield and the two trailing
yields, so cancellation semantics are unchanged.

`agent_identity_metadata` / `agent_citation_metadata` move along (aliased
back into proxy_service). Tests that patched `proxy_service.log_usage`,
`finalize_agent_run`, `release_code_interpreter_turn` or
`AsyncSessionLocal` now also patch the same names on `turn_settlement`,
where the calls live.

proxy_service: 2166 -> 1976 lines. 1371 tests, mypy/vulture/ruff clean.

